    "biography": {
      "concept": "Keeper of the stilt-hall, neutral ground for three Drowned South channels (Act 2-3)",
      "notes": "Sal Tench keeps the stilt-hall where three channels of the Drowned South come to argue. It is neutral ground, and there is a knife-notched tally post by the door. Sal speaks slowly and not much, and most of it is about moorings. Sal will not be hurried by anyone who arrived by punt, counts the moorings before answering anything, and touches the tally post going in and out like a doorframe. Sal is not a bandit and is not not a bandit. Sal is the hall."
    }
